    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on speed and high-leverage top-of-the-order matchups. Our strongest play is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (81.26), whose elite sprint speed makes him an essential start against Dobbins. The combination of a favorable matchup and a dynamic platoon advantage (R/L) pushes **Pete Crow-Armstrong** well into our \"Strong\" tier. He is joined at the top of the order by **Kyle Schwarber** (60.40) and **Yordan Alvarez** (65.52). While **Yordan Alvarez** faces a tougher arm in Woo, his elite xwOBA of .465 provides a high enough floor to anchor the lineup, while **Kyle Schwarber** benefits from the leadoff spot and a moderate matchup against Kremer. **Junior Caminero** (62.27) rounds out our top-tier producers, despite a slightly difficult park factor, as his presence in the three-hole against Rogers ensures premium run-production opportunities.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Caleb Durbin**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a score of 48.55. While **Caleb Durbin** remains an elite stolen base asset, the optimizer prioritized the higher cumulative efficiency scores of **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** and **Colt Keith**, both of whom are projected for more consistent contact against their respective opponents. Meanwhile, we are exercising caution with **Gary Sanchez** (41.24); his score is depressed by a difficult matchup against Skubal, an elite arm with a 2.77 xERA. While **Gary Sanchez** remains in the lineup to preserve our game caps at the catcher position, he sits near the bottom of our efficiency hierarchy today. We will continue to monitor the weather and final lineups for **Pedro Ramirez** and **Kazuma Okamoto**, as any late-breaking shifts in the batting order could necessitate a pivot to our bench options to avoid the sub-40 floor.",
